  "id": "DrugBank_DB00663 - MONDO_4980",
  "verbalization": "Flumethasone, a corticosteroid, is implicated in the treatment of atopic eczema through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Flumethasone is linked to neurodermatitis and contact dermatitis, both of which are inflammatory skin conditions that can progress to atopic eczema. The shared use of prednicarbate, a corticosteroid analog, in these conditions provides a mechanistic link, as prednicarbate is known to suppress inflammation and reduce skin irritation. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and significant relationship between Flumethasone and Atopic Eczema, suggesting that the drug may exert its therapeutic effect through a common pathway involving inflammation regulation. The integration of these paths highlights the role of corticosteroids in modulating inflammatory responses, which is a recurring mechanism in the treatment of atopic eczema.",
